<title>UK: Berkeley places shares at 715 pence each.</title>
<headline>Berkeley places shares at 715 pence each.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British housebuilder and property developer Berkeley Group Plc said on Friday it had placed 4.75 million new ordinary shares of 25 pence each at a price of 715 pence each.</p>
<p>The shares represents around five percent of Berkeley's new ordinary share capital.</p>
<p>The company had earlier said that it would be using the money, around 33.96 million stg, to finance proposed acquisitions.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
